&lt;p&gt;GitLab is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. GitLab’s policies and practices relating to recruitment, employment, career development and advancement, promotion, and retirement are based solely on merit, regardless of race, color, religion, ancestry, sex (including pregnancy, lactation, sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression), national origin, age, citizenship, marital status, mental or physical disability, genetic information (including family medical history), discharge status from the military, protected veteran status (which includes disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, active duty wartime or campaign badge veterans, and Armed Forces service medal veterans), or any other basis protected by law. GitLab will not tolerate discrimination or harassment based on any of these characteristics. See also&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#equal-employment-opportunity-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;GitLab’s EEO Policy&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/labor-and-employment-notices/#eeoc-us-equal-employment-opportunity-commission-notices&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;EEO is the Law&lt;/a&gt;. If you have a disability or special need that requires&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#reasonable-accommodation&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;accommodation&lt;/a&gt;, please let us know during the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/interviewing/#adjustments-to-our-interview-process&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;recruiting process&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting directly to the VP Technology, you&#39;ll build new capability for Awin with AI at the core, free from the constraints of our established delivery model. You&#39;ll take ideas from concept to production quickly, prove what works, and turn the best of it into patterns the wider engineering organisation can adopt.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work closely with product and commercial leaders to find where AI changes the economics of our affiliate marketing platform: what we can build, how fast, and at what cost. You&#39;ll be hands-on most of the time, writing code, shipping and measuring results, rather than coordinating others.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll know enough of our existing platform to connect new things to it safely, but you won&#39;t be absorbed into running it. Your job is to show what modern, AI-native engineering looks like at Awin, and make it real.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is a step-up opportunity.&lt;/strong&gt; We&#39;re looking for a bright, self-starting engineer who is ready for more scope than their current role allows. You might not have held a principal title yet. What matters is that you&#39;re already building this way, you learn fast, and you want the room to prove it. You&#39;ll have direct access to senior leadership, real problems with commercial weight, and the freedom to choose how you solve them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key tasks and accountabilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build and ship&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build and run AI-powered products, tools and services from prototype to production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own outcomes end to end: problem framing, architecture, implementation, evaluation, release and operation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run fast, time-boxed experiments; scale what works and stop what doesn&#39;t, with the evidence to back either call&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set up and evolve the AI infrastructure these builds rely on: model access, evaluation tooling, observability and guardrails&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape direction&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the VP Technology to set Awin&#39;s engineering-specific AI direction, grounded in what has actually been built and measured&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scope strategic opportunities early with product and commercial leaders, with effort, cost and value made explicit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make clear recommendations on build vs buy, model and vendor choice, and where AI should not be used&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Architecture and design&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design new capability so it connects safely to the existing platform: APIs, events, data and identity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Select tools and technologies, and define the patterns and practices for AI-native development at Awin&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Weigh long-term maintainability, economic viability and reuse against speed, and document the trade-offs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Spread what works&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn proven builds into reusable patterns, templates and internal tools, and share them so other teams can adopt them without hand-holding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ways of working&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Works autonomously, guided by the VP Technology&#39;s priorities rather than team-level delivery processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engages directly with engineering, product, data, security and commercial stakeholders as each build requires&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills &amp;amp; Expertise&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI-native engineering&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Builds with coding agents (e.g. Claude Code, Cursor, Codex) as the default way of working. Can show how they decompose work, manage context and review agent output to get production-quality code at pace&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has shipped LLM-powered features to production: prompt and context engineering, tool use and function calling, structured outputs, retrieval (RAG) and multi-step agent workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Builds evaluations first: test sets, automated evals and regression checks for non-deterministic behaviour, with quality measured before and after release&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connects models to enterprise systems and data safely, e.g. MCP servers, internal APIs and event streams, with clear permissions and audit trails&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understands model selection, token economics, latency, caching and fallback strategies, and can explain cost and benefit trade-offs to commercial stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designs for AI-specific security and privacy risks: prompt injection, data leakage, PII handling under GDPR, and guardrails on what models can do&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engineering foundations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert in at least one modern language (Python or TypeScript ideal), and able to work in our existing Java, PHP and JavaScript estate when integrating&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cloud-native and serverless architecture on AWS, with infrastructure as code (Terraform)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with event-driven and distributed systems (Kafka/MSK, SQS/SNS) and with relational and non-relational data stores&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Builds observability into everything: tracing, logging and monitoring, including LLM-specific telemetry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Treats automated testing, CI/CD and secure-by-default design as standard, and automates as much of the delivery loop as possible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ways of building&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Takes an idea to a working prototype in days, then hardens it for production, and knows when to stop&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leaves behind reusable patterns, templates and internal tools, not one-off solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Soft skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
